  "body": "Stacked on #1005 (refreshed against main at f3dd45c4; base branch content: `issue/894-thread-mill`). This PR targets `main`, so until #1005 merges its diff also shows #1005's commits - the #992 change is this branch's own commits only. **It must merge together with #1005, or right after it**: #1005's thread mill without this law posts a non-centre-cutting mill into an undrilled hole, and this PR does not build without #1005.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\n\nA thread mill is not centre-cutting, and the #1005 ride feeds it down the hole's axis at plunge feed. Nothing checked that an earlier operation had opened the hole, so a forgotten tap drill posted a thread mill into solid metal. Now:\n\n- **Generate refuses an undrilled hole by name** (`crates/app/src/operation/thread_entry.rs`, called from the Thread arm of `operation::generate`). Each threaded hole is read in the stock the setup's earlier operations leave standing - the same lazily cut prior grid the drilling and rapid laws read (`drill_prior::PriorCell`). The stock over the hole's minor circle (less one grid cell, never narrower than the mill) must stand at or below the lowest point the path takes the mill to in that hole. Otherwise: \"the hole at (x, y) is not drilled yet: the stock the program ahead leaves stands at z .. inside it, above the thread mill's lowest point at z .. - a thread mill does not cut at its centre - add a drilling operation of at least the .. mm minor diameter, deep enough for its point, before the thread\".\n- **Unknown is refused, never read as air**: nothing ahead cut, a program ahead the grid cannot cut, a posed Thread, a distrusted carried prior, a hole off the grid.\n- **Reordering**: an unposed op's stamp already digests the program ahead (#109), so moving the Drill after the Thread marks the Thread Stale, and regenerating it refuses. Pinned, no new stamp code.\n- Test fixtures: the #894 thread suites' shared fixtures moved to `crates/app/tests/thread_support/mod.rs`. The modelled hole now runs to z 4 (the tap drill's depth), deeper than the thread's floor at z 8, and every thread there has a Drill operation ahead. `mill2d_c`'s R10 thread gets a 20 mm drill ahead. The MCP thread test now pins generate's refusal on the undrilled block.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/992-thread-undrilled.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `camcraft-app --test thread_entry` (new, 5): `a_thread_with_nothing_drilled_ahead_is_refused_by_name`, `a_tap_drill_ahead_opens_the_hole_and_the_thread_verifies_clean` (generator verdict, post gate and program sim clean), `a_drill_of_the_mills_own_diameter_opens_the_hole_too`, `a_drill_too_narrow_or_too_shallow_is_refused`, `moving_the_drill_after_the_thread_marks_it_stale_and_refuses_it` (Stale, post gate shut, regeneration refused, undo restores Ok).\n- `camcraft-app` (lib): `operation::thread_entry::tests::*` (4): drilled/exact-depth air, solid / shallow / narrow refusals by name, unknown prior and off-grid refusals, a hole the path never enters.\n- Updated: `--test thread_mill` (all 8, now drilled first), `--test thread_mill_rim` (all 11) and `--test coarse_rims` thread test (main's #1071/#1073 thread tests: the hole is opened ahead by a flat end-mill Bore of the same declared holes), `--test hole_wall_flats` and `posted_gates/thread` (tap drill ahead), `--test mill2d_c` `thread_helices_are_timed_by_the_tools_pitch`, `--test mcp` `thread_milling_over_the_tools`.\n\nQuick gate (refresh onto #1005 @ f3dd45c4 + upstream/main b0e29114, head `6dd3f773`): `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` - tools, sim, motion, app (every suite) and ui suites, 5 steps, 0 failed (17.4 min). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean (a test-only `Copy` lint fixed after the gate; `--test thread_mill_rim` re-run green, 11/11).\n\nGoldens: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/thread_mill_m8_multi_form.nc` moved - the program now carries the Drill operation ahead (`G81 ... Z4 R20`) and the thread mill is T02; the thread's own blocks are byte-identical. No CL golden moved.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- A stock that already has the hole cored (a FromModel stock) with nothing ahead is refused, not acquitted (decision 3; cheap to add later).\n- Posed (3+2) thread milling is refused by this law (no frame-aware prior reading).\n- The milled Bore ride's axis entry has the same gap: filed as #1036.\n- The heavy `--ignored` release lanes; posts other than Fanuc.\n\nChangelog: A Thread operation whose hole the program ahead has not drilled (to the minor diameter, below the thread) is refused by name at generate instead of feeding a non-centre-cutting thread mill into solid stock (#992).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #992\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
